#
# .hypatia-ignore — repo-scoped exemptions for the estate governance
# bundle's anti-pattern scanner. Format (per the bundle's `is_exempt`
# function): each non-comment line is `${rule}:${path}` matched as a
# fixed-string whole-line equality (`grep -qxF`).
#
# Comment lines (`#`) and blank lines are tolerated because they never
# match the `rule:path` shape under -xF.

# ─── Gossamer's vendored Android platform shell (third_party/) ─────────
#
# third_party/gossamer/android/src/main/java/io/gossamer/{GossamerActivity,
# GossamerBridge}.java are part of the vendored Gossamer webview shell
# (third_party/gossamer/), not paint-type's own source. The estate's
# "Kotlin is goodbye" policy targets hand-written JVM bindings written
# BY a project's own FFI/interop layer; Android's platform contract
# itself requires a JVM-hosted Activity + WebView bridge class regardless
# of implementation language underneath (Gossamer's own core is Zig/Rust
# per its architecture — these two files are the unavoidable Android
# platform glue, not a policy violation of paint-type's own tier mapping).
# Rewriting vendored upstream code to route around a shell policy is out
# of scope and not owned by paint-type; the exemption travels with the
# vendored copy.
cicd_rules/banned_language_file:third_party/gossamer/android/src/main/java/io/gossamer/GossamerActivity.java
cicd_rules/banned_language_file:third_party/gossamer/android/src/main/java/io/gossamer/GossamerBridge.java

# ─── TWO CONSUMERS, TWO MATCHERS — read this before adding a line ──────
#
# The header above describes the governance bundle's matcher only. This
# file is read by two independent consumers and they do NOT agree:
#
#   1. the estate governance bundle (governance-reusable.yml:473,630)
#        grep -qxF "${rule}:${f}"   -> whole-line EQUALITY, exact path
#   2. Hypatia's own scanner (Hypatia.ScannerSuppression, scanner_suppression.ex)
#        String.contains?(rel, fragment) -> the repo-relative path CONTAINS
#        the fragment, so a directory prefix ending in "/" is valid here
#        and inert for consumer 1.
#
# Consequence: the two entries above are exact paths for consumer 1 and are
# inert for consumer 2 — Hypatia refuses to suppress `banned_language_file`
# at all, by design. The entry below is the mirror image: a directory
# fragment for consumer 2, inert for consumer 1.
#
# ⚠ The fragment is UNANCHORED. `x/third_party/gossamer/` would also match.
# Acceptable here because no such path exists in this repo; it would not be
# acceptable for a fragment that could collide.

# ─── Gossamer's vendored Idris2 proof code (third_party/) ──────────────
#
# Hypatia's two `critical` findings on this repo are both
# code_safety/believe_me in VENDORED Gossamer proof sources:
#   third_party/gossamer/.../abi/PanelIsolation.idr
#   third_party/gossamer/.../Gossamer/ABI/PanelIsolation.idr
# `believe_me` is an Idris2 escape hatch in upstream code paint-type does
# not own and must not rewrite. Scoped to the rule, NOT to the directory:
# measured on the real 179-finding artifact, this line suppresses exactly
# 2 findings and leaves 177 — including 39 other findings inside
# third_party/gossamer/ under other rules, which still report.
code_safety/believe_me:third_party/gossamer/
